The '''Sunwell Plateau''' is a raid instance located on the [[Isle of Quel'Danas (Burning Crusade)|Isle of Quel'Danas]] north of [[Silvermoon City]].

==Background==
{{main|Sunwell}}
[[File:Sunwell Plateau creation.jpg|thumb|upright|[[Dath'Remar Sunstrider]] and his followers creating Sunwell Plateau.]]
Around 6,800 [[BDP]], the [[Highborne]] exiles under the leadership of [[Dath'Remar Sunstrider]] arrived at the forested woodlands one day known as [[Quel'Thalas]]. Unveiling a stolen vial of water from the [[Well of Eternity]], he poured its contents into a lake situated at a convergence of powerful [[ley line]]s, the [[Sunwell Grove]]. A brilliant fount of energy tore through the skies of [[Azeroth]], and Dath'Remar proclaimed that this new source of power would one day surpass its predecessor. They then used their magic to create the plateau around the fount of power.<ref>''[[The Sunwell Trilogy Ultimate Edition]]''</ref> The [[Sunwell]] was named after Dath'Remar, in honor of his bold quest to reignite Highborne culture, and over time, his followers would become known as the [[High elf|high elves]].<ref>{{Ref WoWCV1|120|121}}</ref>

===Third War===
{{Novel-section}}
During the [[Scourge invasion of Quel'Thalas]] in 20 [[ADP]], [[Ranger-General]] [[Sylvanas Windrunner]] sent the young [[Elven ranger|ranger]] [[Tel'kor]] to the Sunwell Plateau to warn the mages that they could have been betrayed,<ref>''[[Arthas: Rise of the Lich King]]'', chapter 18</ref> however, [[Dar'Khan Drathir]] had already lowered the shields surrounding the [[Sunwell]]. Having betrayed his kin to aid [[Arthas Menethil]], the treacherous Dar'Khan proceeded by killing key members of the [[Convocation of Silvermoon]] present within the plateau, and bound the well's energies using instructions from his undead masters.<ref>[[The Warcraft Encyclopedia/High Elves]]</ref>

When [[Kael'thas Sunstrider|Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider]] returned from [[Dalaran]], he discovered that the greatest danger to his people was not the [[Scourge]] remnants, but the corrupted Sunwell. With the aid of the most powerful remaining magi, the prince executed a plan that would irrevocably change the fate of his people and succeeded in destroying the Sunwell through a great ritual.<ref>''[[Blood of the Highborne]]'', chapter 3</ref>

===The Burning Crusade===
{{Bc-section}}
[[File:Sunwell Plateau.jpg|thumb|left|The gates of Sunwell Plateau near [[Sun's Reach]].]]
During the [[Battle for Quel'Danas]] in 27 ADP, heroes from [[Shattrath City]] joined under the banner of the [[Shattered Sun Offensive]], endeavoring to crush the [[Burning Legion]]'s invasion before it became insurmountable. More combatants joined the Offensive every day, but the might of the Legion could not be easily suppressed. Fierce demonic servants guarded the Sunwell Plateau, attacking anyone who interfered with their proceedings. As the time of [[Kil'jaeden]]'s arrival drew near, Azeroth's heroes had one final chance to save their world from blistering devastation.<ref>[http://us.battle.net/wow/en/zone/the-sunwell/ The Sunwell]</ref>

The Offensive's efforts delayed [[Kael'thas Sunstrider|Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider]]' spellwork long enough for [[Alliance]] adventurers to infiltrate the Sunwell Plateau, where they fought against Legion demons, [[Sunfury]] elves, and [[Felblood elf|felblood elves]]. They also rescued and defeated prisoners such as the [[blue dragon]] [[Kalecgos]], controlled by the [[nathrezim]] [[Sathrovarr the Corruptor|Sathrovarr]], and the [[naaru]] [[M'uru]]. Entering the Sunwell chamber, Kil'jaeden rose from a rift in the fount's depths before the heroes' eyes. They fought hard, but it was eventually [[Anveena Teague]] who turned the tide when she sacrificed herself, using her remaining energy against the demon lord. The adventurers then managed to banish the weakened Kil'jaeden and close the gateway.<ref>[[Kil'jaeden (tactics)]]</ref>

However, the Sunwell laid tainted again, threatening to corrupt blood elves once more. Although [[Lor'themar Theron|Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron]] considered destroying the corrupted Sunwell, another solution presented itself when [[Velen|Prophet Velen]] arrived in the halls, paying respects to the fallen naaru M'uru. The prophet sensed in its heart a glimmer of power and used it to cleanse the Sunwell, transforming it into a font of [[Light|Holy Light]] and [[arcane]] magic.<ref>{{Ref WoWCV3|159}}</ref> In the wake of Kil'jaeden's fall, a lot of powerful artifacts were found and stored.<ref>''[[World of Warcraft: Exploring Azeroth: The Eastern Kingdoms]]'', pg. 95</ref>

===Wrath of the Lich King===
{{Wotlk-section}}
By the time of the [[war against the Lich King|Scourgewar]] in 27 ADP, a number of high elves had been permitted to make pilgrimages to the restored fount of power, with [[Captain Auric Sunchaser]] as their representative.<ref>[[Warden of the Sunwell]]</ref>

===Battle for Azeroth===
{{Bfa-section}}
After the [[Argus Campaign]] in 32 ADP, the Sunwell Plateau was visited by [[Lor'themar Theron]], [[Grand Magister Rommath]], [[First Arcanist Thalyssra]], [[Arcanist Valtrois]], [[Silgryn]], and [[Alleria Windrunner]]. The visit was intended as a gesture of goodwill for the [[nightborne]] leaders and courtesy for Alleria; while the latter was estranged from Silvermoon's political climate, Lor'themar would not deny a daughter of Quel'Thalas' request to see their people's most sacred site. However, Alleria's presence attracted a group of [[void]] creatures, who invaded the plateau at [[Nether-Prince Durzaan]]'s command and began spreading their corruption. The heroes, along with the Sunwell's magi, wardens, and [[Spellbreakers]], repelled the abomination until a powerful void horror, [[Aruun the Darkener]], emerged in an attempt to contaminate the well directly but was stopped and killed. Finally, a rift portal was opened directly above the Sunwell's waters, but Rommath, Thalyssra, and Alleria combined their magics to close it before catastrophe struck. In the aftermath of the battle, Alleria was exiled by Lor'themar on the grounds that her very presence poses a threat to Quel'Thalas and the Sunwell. The battle's outcome also endeared the regent to Thalyssra, who pledged the [[Suramar (kingdom)|kingdom of Suramar]] to the [[Horde]].<ref>[[Remember the Sunwell]]</ref>

During the [[Fourth War]] in 33 ADP, as part of a [[Heritage of the Sin'dorei|ceremony of remembrance]] held each year in the kingdom, the [[blood elf]] [[adventurer]] returned to the Sunwell on their journey to reenact the [[Scourge invasion of Quel'Thalas]]. The adventurer inevitably failed to prevent [[Arthas]]' advance into the plateau and the corruption of the Sunwell, and then experienced the aftermath of the onslaught, when [[Kael'thas Sunstrider|Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider]] led a raid to destroy the tainted fount of power and save his race from destruction.<ref>[[The Fall of the Sunwell]]</ref>

===Midnight===
{{Mn-section}}
When [[Xal'atath]] and her [[Void]] forces invaded Quel'Danas, the blood elf forces led by [[Lady Liadrin]] and [[Lor'themar Theron]] made their stand here, with the two leaders defending the Sunwell on one of the plateau's walls. During the battle, Lady Liadrin summoned the [[Army of the Light]] to aid them.<ref>[[Intercession]]</ref> The Sunwell Plateau will be revisited in the [[March on Quel'Danas (instance)|March on Quel'Danas]] raid.

