==Notes and trivia==
*When exactly the Plateau complex was constructed is unknown, and there are conflicting sources:
**The site of the Sunwell was first seen in ''Warcraft III''. [[The Fall of Silvermoon (WC3 Undead)|The Fall of Silvermoon]] mission has the Sunwell in the center of Silvermoon City, despite the fact that the Sunwell Grove was present on maps.
***''[[Warcraft III: Reforged]]'' changes the map in that mission to more closely match its appearance in ''World of Warcraft'', including putting the Sunwell on an island north of Silvermoon. Notably, the updated ''Reforged'' map has the Sunwell out in the open, not inside the Sunwell Plateau building.
** ''[[The Sunwell Trilogy Ultimate Edition]]'' depicts [[Dath'Remar Sunstrider]] and his followers magically creating the structures around the Sunwell right after the Sunwell itself was made.
**In ''[[Arthas: Rise of the Lich King]]'', [[Sylvanas Windrunner]] sent [[Tel'kor]] to the Sunwell Plateau, and it mentions that Arthas managed to reach the plateau, but it doesn't elaborate on any structures except for the Sunwell pool itself.
**The [[Fury of the Sunwell trailer]], showing the Sunwell before and during the Third War, is in an open space.
**''[[The Sunwell Trilogy]]'' depicts Dar'Khan killing his colleagues and Sunwell's destruction during the Third War by Dar'Khan, with some structures around the Sunwell. The third part shows the Sunwell area as a crater, with some structures further away.
**''[[Blood of the Highborne]]'' mentions that Dar'Khan killed the magisters of the Convocation of Silvermoon in the Sunwell Plateau, but it doesn't elaborate on any structures. Later, when Kael and his companions were working their magic to destroy the corrupted Sunwell, no structures were mentioned either; instead, they were in an open area with rain pouring on the elves, undead, trolls, and ground around the Sunwell.
**The overall structure of the raid itself implies that the Scourge fought through multiple gates to reach the Sunwell, or that (perhaps less likely) the blood elf forces loyal to the Burning Legion magically built the walls over the Dead Scar, which caused them to instantly decay.
**In ''Reforged'', the map is completely overhauled from its ''Warcraft III'' version and shows one gate and otherwise open space with trees around the Sunwell.
<!-- ***In [[Warcraft III/Patch 1.32.10|patch 1.32.10]], the Sunwell area was updated to contain structures around the Sunwell. -->
**The [[Heritage of the Sin'dorei]], that depicts the events of ''Blood of the Highborne'' (Kael destroying the corrupted Sunwell), occurs in the Sunwell Plateau raid map.
**''[[All That is Sacred]]'' depicts the structure existing when [[Liadrin]] was a child.
*Nearly every mob in the instance has the [[Sunwell Radiance]] buff, increasing melee hit by 5% and reducing opposing chance to dodge by 20%.
*A [[Sunwell Plateau epilogue|scripted event]] will occur after Kil'jaeden's defeat.
*There is a [[Scrying Orb (Magisters' Terrace)|Scrying Orb]] found on a balcony in the [[Magisters' Terrace (Burning Crusade)|Magisters' Terrace]] past the second boss that gives a sneak peek of the nearby Sunwell Plateau raid.
*The architecture of the Sunwell Plateau is comparable to that of [[Silvermoon City]].
*Before [[World of Warcraft: Wrath of the Lich King|''Wrath of the Lich King'']] came out, less than one percent of the playerbase actually experienced Sunwell.<ref>[http://www.mmo-champion.com/content/2688-Other-Press-Tour-Interviews-A-Night-in-Mists-of-Pandaria-Blue-Posts-MoP-Screenshot Other Press Tour Interviews, A Night in Mists of Pandaria, Blue Posts, MoP Screenshot]</ref>

